--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/semantic-preview.md
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Candidate incremental semantic preview API
+
+This local candidate change is based on 8cadfede7063c896b944e7bae05daa3549ae97ea.
+It adds observations without changing protocol output/finish behavior.
+
+`StreamProcessor` now owns a `SemanticSessionHandle` pointing to an explicit
+synchronous `SemanticSession`. Canonical token decode + parser feed is one
+synchronous step. No mutex guard spans a protocol generator await. The Python
+binding retains the handle before consuming the processor into its async stream;
+its existing mutex serializes push/drain and preview at the next-input boundary.
+Rust callers must likewise serialize input and preview at an input boundary.
+
+`SemanticSession` forks only StateMachine and decoder mutable state: parser stage,
+KMP prefixes/tables, stashed byte count, reasoning/newline/JSON state, pending
+IDs/count, absolute decoded byte offset and first terminal observation. No
+protocol generator, stashed protocol chunks, async input channel or generated
+history is cloned. Protocol stashing still consumes the exact original actions.
+
+The decode implementation is shared using Arc<Mutex<Box<dyn TokenizerDecoder>>>;
+the mutex preserves the existing Send-only trait bound. The tokenizer itself is
+not copied. Decode still calls decode_ids(pending_ids, false), holds empty text or
+text ending in U+FFFD, and resets pending state only on a successful text flush.
+Custom decoders opt in to preview only if immutable and deterministic; the default
+supports_semantic_preview is false. The standard Tokenizer and its Arc delegate
+opt in. Unsupported custom decoding returns inexact mapping and zero safe count,
+without calling that decoder. Missing tokenizer/decode errors return an error.
+
+The StateMachine records the actual matched transition into Finished. The
+additional semantic observation distinguishes STOP_SEQUENCE from
+DSML_TOOL_CALL_BLOCK_END, and records an absolute half-open decoded-byte span.
+DSML opening or invocation closure is not terminal; JSON fence closure is not
+terminal. `finished` retains its original protocol stream meaning. DSML terminal
+metadata does not close the stream or invent a backend finish reason.
+
+Python:
+
+```python
+result = processor.preview_tokens(candidate_ids)
+result.terminal_kind             # None, STOP_SEQUENCE, DSML_TOOL_CALL_BLOCK_END
+result.completing_token_index    # None or zero-based candidate index
+result.safe_token_count          # candidate IDs before completing token
+result.source_start              # None or absolute decoded-source byte position
+result.source_end                # None or exclusive end
+result.mapping_exact             # false => caller must fail closed
+result.candidate_ids_processed
+result.max_pending_ids
+processor.semantic_terminal      # actual canonical observation, not preview
+```
+
+A flush caused by candidate j can include IDs pending before preview. Its first
+terminal transition maps exactly to j under the canonical decoder contract.
+Earlier candidate IDs that produced no text remain in the safe prefix. Span start
+can precede this call. The result never re-tokenizes decoded text or rounds byte
+positions forward. No terminal yields safe count equal to candidate count.
+Already-terminal/ended session yields mapping_exact=false and safe count zero;
+closed/finished Python streams reject preview. Canonical semantic metadata is
+readable after normal protocol completion, but not after close/error.
+
+The fork stops after the first terminal-producing flush. The authoritative feed
+may consume the entire flush including an invalid tail, exactly as canonical feed
+does; the returned span remains the first terminal byte span and the completing
+candidate must remain outside any speculative target-committed drained prefix.
+
+State-copy cost is independent of generated history length, but proportional to
+configured matcher patterns and pending IDs. The existing decoder contract can
+retain an arbitrarily long group if decoding never produces a usable flush; this
+change does not promise a fixed maximum pending size. Callers may impose separate
+eligibility/resource bounds, not change detokenization.
+
+Tests: `cargo test -p deepseek-recipe`, plus
+`deepseek-recipe-python/tests/test_semantic_preview.py` after a real native build.
+The consuming ds41f M31 source driver compares raw outputs and chat events against
+the pristine pinned source. Python/native and live MTP qualification are separate
+prerequisites; this extension alone does not authorize speculative serving.
-- 
2.50.1


